{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Who came to Egypt: seventy.</b> Joseph and his two sons and Yocheved are included, and the verse follows the majority — and so the way of many verses. This is the principle: Jacob, and no woman was included except Dinah, Yocheved, Serach, and Hetzron and Chamul and Hever and Malkiel were included. According to the one who says that twin sisters were born with the tribes, as Rashi explained — from where do we know that they died before their descent to Egypt? One may answer: from the fact that את is not written for any of the tribes in the entire passage, but only for Dinah — this implies that all of them (the twin sisters) died, except Dinah's, who survived."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {0 "The final word השלימה is read as 'she remained/survived' (from שלם, to remain), fitting the argument that Dinah's twin alone survived; the text is somewhat obscure and read hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:50.411516920Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}